<title>AUSTRIA: OMV 1996 earnings, dividend up.</title>
<headline>OMV 1996 earnings, dividend up.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for the year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>						1996	   1995</p>
<p> Group sales			     78,269	73,299</p>
<p> Group earnings before interest     2,921   vs  2,191</p>
<p>and tax (EBIT)</p>
<p> Group pre-tax			    2,974   vs  2,092</p>
<p> Group net				  1,981   vs  1,731</p>
<p> Dividend (schillings)		     23   vs     20</p>
<p> Group cash flow (billion schillings)5.28   vs   7.86</p>
<p> Group workforce			  8,491   vs  9,659</p>
<p> Group personnel costs		  7,192   vs  7,605</p>
<p> Investment (bln schillings)	   6.43	  3.95</p>
<p>Earnings before interest and tax by sector</p>
<p>(bln schillings)</p>
<p> E&amp;P					   0.25	 (0.39)</p>
<p> Gas					   1.77	  1.73</p>
<p> Refining				    0.12	  0.62</p>
<p> Marketing				   0.12	 (0.06)</p>
<p> Plastics				    0.51	  0.30</p>
<p> Chemicals				   0.50	  0.40</p>
<p>Sales by sector</p>
<p>(bln schillings)</p>
<p> E&amp;P					   5.84	  5.06</p>
<p> Gas					  11.34	 10.50</p>
<p> Refining				   42.07	 37.38</p>
<p> Marketing				  21.22	 17.39</p>
<p> Plastics				    9.14	  8.85</p>
<p> Chemicals				   5.21	  8.07</p>
<p>NOTE - OMV AG, Austria's biggest industrial group, posted record pre-tax earnings for the second straight year.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +43-1 531 12 254</p>
</text>
